  "body": "I was implementing something like discovery system using a BroadcastChannel.\r\nMy plan was to use the BroadcastChannel for messaging related to finding available clients, and once the user would like to connect to a specific tab, I wanted to pass a MessagePort over to the other client via the BroadcastChannel.\r\nBut it seems `BroadcastChannel.postMessage()` does not have an argument for a transferList like other `postMessage`s do.\r\nIs there a reason for this? At first I thought it had something to do with different windows not necessarily sharing the same browser process. But I believe transferrable items can already be passed via shared workers. So I'm not sure why this limitation exists.",
